Jonathan “Benjo” Manigo is a Filipino visual artist with over two decades of experience dedicated to the arts. Born November 8, 1973, he works across portraits, landscapes, seascapes, abstracts, cubism, surrealism, still life, and murals.

## Exhibitions and collections

His work has been shown at Festival Mall and Alabang Town Center in Muntinlupa City, and is held in private collections in Makati. He joined the Muntinlupa Art Society in 2000.
